The ZZ background contribution from quark-antiquark annihilation is simulated at NLO pQCD with POWHEG 2.0 [80], while the gg → ZZ process is generated at LO with MCFM 7.0.1 [81]. The WZ background and the triboson backgrounds ZZZ, WZZ, and WWZ are modeled at NLO using MADGRAPH5_aMC@NLO 2.4.2. The smaller t̄Z, t̄WW, and t̄ZZ background processes are simulated at LO with MADGRAPH5_aMC@NLO 2.4.2. The events containing Z bosons with associated jets (Z+jets) are simulated at NLO with MADGRAPH5_aMC@NLO 2.4.2 and the t̄Z background is simulated at NNLO with POWHEG 2.0. The reducible background determination does not rely on the MC but is based on data, as described in Section 7.2.

